GameEngine overlay patch for lexbor 3.0.1.

css/selectors: preserve unknown and known-but-unsupported pseudo-classes
instead of failing the whole selector.

lxb_css_selectors_state_pseudo_class() in source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
looks the pseudo-class name up in lexbor's data table. Two paths used to abort
the selector, and aborting a selector makes lexbor discard the entire style
rule (every comma-separated selector in it, not just the offending one), so no
AST node is ever emitted:

  1. Unknown names (e.g. :loading, :my-state): lxb_css_selector_pseudo_class_by_name
     returns NULL and the function returned lxb_css_parser_unexpected_status.
  2. Known-but-"not supported" names (:visited, :valid, :scope, :target, ...):
     these resolve to a real id but were routed into an explicit switch that
     logged lxb_css_log_not_supported and returned lxb_css_parser_unexpected_status.
     (0001 already trimmed :focus-within / :focus-visible out of this switch.)

The "not supported" branch exists because lexbor's own DOM selector-matching
engine does not implement those pseudo-classes. GameEngine never uses that
engine: it uses lexbor only to build the selector AST, then matches with its
own cascade engine (Engine/Modules/UI). So both rejections only served to
silently drop rules the engine is perfectly able to match.

This patch:

  - Replaces the NULL bail with: stamp the node's pseudo type as
    LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS__UNDEF (0x0000, a valid data-table entry),
    clear its data, consume the token, and return LXB_STATUS_OK — mirroring the
    known-pseudo success path immediately below. The dup'd name text on
    selector->name is preserved, so the engine's converter recovers the state
    name from it. CSSStylesheetParser.cpp::ConvertPseudoSimple maps any
    unmapped pseudo id (including __UNDEF) through its `default:` branch to
    PseudoClass::Kind::Custom with CustomName = lowercased selector name — so
    :loading / :my-state parse as ordinary custom-state pseudo-classes. The
    engine computes its own specificity from the converted chain and never
    serializes selectors back through lexbor, so an __UNDEF node never re-enters
    lexbor logic.

  - Deletes the known-but-"not supported" switch entirely, so :visited /
    :valid / :scope / :target / etc. fall through to the same success path as
    :hover / :focus and reach the engine as Kind::Custom rather than killing
    their rules. The now-unused `msg` local is removed with it.

Unknown FUNCTIONAL pseudo-classes — :foo(...) — are deliberately left
unsupported: lxb_css_selectors_state_pseudo_class_function still rejects them,
because accepting a functional pseudo requires an argument-consuming state
machine to balance its parentheses. That is out of scope here; only the
argument-less simple pseudo-class path is relaxed.

When upstream vcpkg bumps the lexbor version, resync this portfile, vcpkg.json,
and re-cut both patches against the new source (this hunk targets
lxb_css_selectors_state_pseudo_class in source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c;
cut 0002 against the 0001-patched tree since vcpkg applies patches in order).

diff --git a/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c b/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
--- a/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
+++ b/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
@@ -1443,7 +1443,6 @@ lxb_css_selectors_state_pseudo_class(lxb_css_parser_t *parser,
                                      const lxb_css_syntax_token_t *token)
 {
     lxb_status_t status;
-    lxb_css_log_message_t *msg;
     lxb_css_selector_t *selector;
     lxb_css_selectors_t *selectors;
     const lxb_css_selectors_pseudo_data_t *pseudo;
@@ -1458,38 +1457,12 @@ lxb_css_selectors_state_pseudo_class(lxb_css_parser_t *parser,
     pseudo = lxb_css_selector_pseudo_class_by_name(selector->name.data,
                                                    selector->name.length);
     if (pseudo == NULL) {
-        return lxb_css_parser_unexpected_status(parser);
-    }
+        selector->u.pseudo.type = LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS__UNDEF;
+        selector->u.pseudo.data = NULL;
 
-    switch (pseudo->id) {
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_CURRENT:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_DEFAULT:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FULLSCREEN:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FUTURE:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_IN_RANGE:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_INDETERMINATE:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_INVALID:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_LOCAL_LINK:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_OUT_OF_RANGE:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_PAST:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_SCOPE:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_TARGET:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_TARGET_WITHIN:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_USER_INVALID:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_VALID:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_VISITED:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_WARNING:
-            msg = lxb_css_log_not_supported(parser->log,
-                                            lxb_css_selectors_module_name,
-                                            (const char *) selector->name.data);
-            if (msg == NULL) {
-                return lxb_css_parser_memory_fail(parser);
-            }
-
-            return lxb_css_parser_unexpected_status(parser);
+        lxb_css_syntax_parser_consume(parser);
 
-        default:
-            break;
+        return LXB_STATUS_OK;
     }
 
     selector->u.pseudo.type = pseudo->id;
